  "body": "Release branch for **v0.18.0** (minor: 34 `feat` commits since v0.17.0, breaking: none). Cut from main `f490458a`, plus main `bab6a0c0` (PR #1003, the gate's own re-measured pin) merged in.\n\n## What is on this branch\n- `docs: 0.18.0 release notes; changelog` - `RELEASE_NOTES.md` (0.18.0 on top, history kept below), 50 changelog rows for the behaviour PRs merged since v0.17.0, and the per-PR decision files gathered into `RECOMMENDED.md` (`cargo xtask decisions --version 0.18.0`; 57 files, `docs/decisions/` keeps its README).\n- `test(ui): regenerate the snapshot goldens for 0.18.0` - the three shell goldens (dark, light, tool editor). **The maintainer accepted them for this cut without the usual manual look at the diff images** (2026-11-12, said before going offline). The orchestrator looked at the new images: they render a sane UI; the one regression they show is the truncated ribbon labels and missing group captions since PR 767, filed as issue 948.\n- Notes edits: the Doosan DNM A0 bug (issue 950, P0, filed during the freeze - the post is new in this release) and the bore regression (issue 980) are listed under Known issues.\n- `chore(release): 0.18.0 - release` and `sync Cargo.lock` - the version bump, made by `cargo xtask release --version 0.18.0 --no-tag --installer`.\n\n## Gate\n`cargo xtask release` ran the full **release tier** on this tree: 14 steps, 0 failed, 46.5 min (logs `gate-logs/release-20261112-013551/`): geometry, cl, tools, post, kernel, sim, motion, app, ui, clippy `-D warnings`, the motion and app heavy lanes (release, `--ignored`), the ui snapshot lane and the gpu_render snapshot lane.\n\nThe first full run of the tier was red in one heavy-lane test, `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`: since PR 839's finer STEP mesh a second level of the test part falls back from the Adaptive plan to Offset rings (still verified clean, named in the notes). PR #1003 re-measured that pin (test-only, high-tier reviewed) and issue 980 stays open for the planner. That decision was taken by the orchestrator while the maintainer was offline; it is recorded on issue 980, in `RECOMMENDED.md` and in the release notes.\n\n## Built locally\n`dist/camcraft-0.18.0-win-x64.zip` (28.7 MB, 91 files; `post.exe` reports 0.18.0). No installer: Inno Setup (`ISCC.exe`) is not installed on this machine; signing skipped (no certificate). The published artifact is built by `release.yml` from the tag.\n\n## Not exercised\nmacOS / Linux builds; the wasm web runner (not part of the release download); hand-testing of the GUI.\n\n## After merge\nTag the merge commit `v0.18.0` (after checking its tree equals this branch's tip), push the tag (starts `release.yml`), comment `shipped in v0.18.0` on the issues closed since v0.17.0.\n\nChangelog: none (this PR carries the changelog itself).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
